  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite its position as Africa&#x2019;s largest economy, accounting for more than 15% of the continent&#x2019;s Gross Domestic Product (GDP), and a population exceeding 200 million, Nigeria struggles to leverage its strengths to benefit from regional trade and integration. This challenge is evident in the significantly low intra-African trade volumes, which stood at only 4.5 percent in 2022. Harnessing the country&#x2019;s immense potential will require the strengthening of local production value chains, policies, i</narrative>
  </description>
